# Record LLM, tool and reply payloads on agent traces

Context: Graph Chat turns that ended with the "couldn't display that answer"
fallback could not be diagnosed from MLflow: LLM spans only carried token
counts, tool calls produced no span at all, and the agent span had no reply.
The app log also gave no hint of why the final message had no text. Spans now
carry the (truncated) conversation, the model reply with its content block
types and finish reason, and every tool call with its arguments and result.
Graph Chat also logs each iteration's finish reason and warns when the final
message has no readable text.

Changes:

1. src/agents/tracing.py
   LLM spans record max_tokens, tool count, the truncated messages, the reply
   text, content block types, text length and tool calls. Tool spans record
   the truncated result and resolve the tool name / arguments from the call
   signature (works for dispatchers and single tools). Agent spans record the
   final reply. Reasoning blocks appear as `[reasoning]` markers; their
   signatures are never recorded. `ONTOBRICKS_TRACE_PAYLOADS=false` keeps
   sizes only; `ONTOBRICKS_TRACE_MAX_CHARS` (default 4000) caps each field.
2. src/agents/engine_base.py
   `dispatch_tool` is traced, so every agent's tool calls become TOOL spans.
3. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
   Logs finish_reason, completion tokens, content block types and tool-call
   count per iteration, and warns when the final reply has no readable text.
4. tests/units/agents/test_agent_tracing.py
   Coverage for payload summaries, signature redaction, the payload switch,
   tool-call binding and active LLM / tool spans.
5. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py
   Coverage for the unreadable-reply warning.

