================================================================================
Graph explorer entity floor, smaller chat tool results, reverse-edge hash index
================================================================================

Context:
MLflow traces showed Graph Chat turns of 50-190 s with 170k-270k prompt
tokens per question; describe_entity returned 500-triple pages that were
re-sent to the LLM on every later iteration. On Lakebase, BFS reverse-edge
lookups (`object IN (...)`) go through the union view, which does not expose
`object_hash`, so they seq-scan the triple table (EXPLAIN: Seq Scan,
95k rows removed by filter). The explorer could not request fewer than 100
entities.

Changes:
1. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/tools.py
   describe_entity page limit 500 -> 200 triples (`_FIND_PAGE_LIMIT`), and
   describe_entity / query_graphql results capped at 20k chars with a
   "narrow the search" hint (`_cap_result`).
2. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py
   `ensure_graph_indexes` also creates `USING hash (object)` (`*_obj`).
   Hash index has no btree row-size limit, so it is safe on long literals.
   Applied on the next Knowledge Graph build.
3. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_sigmagraph.html
   Max-entities selector gains 50 / 100 / 200; default 5000 -> 500.
4. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Filter-expand entity floor 100 -> 50 so the 50 option is honoured.
5. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat.py,
   tests/units/core/test_lakebase_flat_store.py
   Coverage for the page limit, result truncation and the hash index DDL.

