================================================================================
Graph explorer: honour max entities, show and centre the focused node
================================================================================

Context:
With max entities = 50 the explorer still drew 367 nodes: filter_expand
returned every triple of the capped entity set, including edges to
neighbours outside it, and the viewer turns each edge target into a node.
Opening the explorer on a focus URI (e.g. ?focus=.../SalesTransaction/SAL00677)
neither selected nor centred that node: groups start collapsed, so the
target was hidden inside a one-member "group #N (1)" super-node, and the
render can defer itself before the focus lookup runs.

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   `_drop_out_of_set_edges`: filter_expand keeps literal and rdf:type
   triples, and only relationship triples whose both ends are in the BFS set.
2. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   - One-member group components render as the real instance node.
   - Expanded seed entities are never collapsed into group super-nodes.
   - Focus-by-URI uses the exact URI as seed when found, pins that node at
     the layout centre (`fixed` during ForceAtlas2), and waits for the
     deferred render before selecting it.
   - Max-entities fallback 5000 -> 50.
3. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_sigmagraph.html
   Max-entities default 500 -> 50.
4. tests/units/dtwin/test_filter_expand_bounds.py
   Coverage for dropping out-of-set edges and keeping literals/types.

