================================================================================
Graph Chat fast path: GraphQL inverse fields, filters, counts, schema digest
================================================================================

Context:
MLflow traces (experiment /Shared/ontobricks-agents) showed entity-centric and
filtered questions taking 7-9 LLM iterations (34-44 s). "What did customer X
buy" ran describe_entity depth=2 (35k triples, truncated), guessed entity
types, re-fetched the GraphQL SDL, and only then issued the one useful
salesTransactions(search:...) query. "Customers who bought product P at store
S" guessed the wrong entity type five times, pulled unfiltered 200/500-row
lists that hit the 20k-char tool cap, and reported only a fraction of the
true buyers. Root causes: no inverse GraphQL fields (Customer could not
reach its purchases), list queries only had limit/offset/search, every
forward relationship was resolved eagerly to depth 2 regardless of the
selection, and the system prompt forced describe_entity first (and also told
the agent to use depth >= 2) while the schema was rediscovered every turn.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/graphdb/SubjectFilter.py (new), src/back/core/graphdb/__init__.py
   Backend-neutral AND filter (data contains / relationship target label
   contains or id equals / entity id equals), re-exported from the package.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBBackend.py
   find_subjects_by_type accepts filters; new count_subjects_by_type
   (COUNT DISTINCT subject, or COUNT DISTINCT object of a predicate for
   distinctBy) and find_subjects_by_predicate_objects (reverse-edge lookup:
   predicate = p AND object IN (...), optional rdf:type restriction, row cap).
   Shared by Delta and Lakebase; same _sql_escape quoting as existing SQL.
   Unfiltered SQL is byte-identical to before.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jReadOps.py, src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jStore.py
   Native Cypher implementations of the same three methods (pattern
   comprehension for relationship filters, dynamic property keys for data
   filters). A filter on a predicate the graph never stored matches nothing
   instead of raising.
4. src/back/core/graphql/GraphQLSchemaBuilder.py
   One inverse list field per object property on its range type, named
   <pluralOfDomain>Via<Property> (e.g. Customer.salesTransactionsViaSoldTo);
   skipped on Python/camelCase name collision; self-references and cycles
   build fine. New root field <plural>Count(search, filters, distinctBy) per
   type; root-field name collisions are skipped. TypeInfo now records
   inverse fields, GraphQL names, class / relationship labels and root names.
5. src/back/core/graphql/ResolverFactory.py, src/back/core/graphql/FieldFilter.py (new)
   List resolvers take filters: [FieldFilter!] ({field, value}, AND) and
   pass the strawberry selection tree (fragments merged) to the metadata;
   new count resolver.
6. src/back/core/graphql/SchemaMetadata.py
   Selection-aware resolution: only selected forward / inverse fields are
   loaded, identity-only selections ({ id } / { uri }) skip the triple load,
   selection-aware queries are bounded by the query nesting (MAX_DEPTH)
   instead of DEFAULT_DEPTH. Without selection info the legacy eager
   behaviour is unchanged and inverse fields stay unresolved. Filters are
   validated (unknown field -> ValidationError listing the valid fields);
   filtered lists, counts and inverse lookups raise InfrastructureError
   instead of silently returning []. List limit clamped to 1..1000. The
   "predicate mismatch" warning no longer fires for rdf:type on every entity.
7. src/back/core/graphql/SchemaDigest.py (new), src/back/core/graphql/constants.py,
   src/back/core/graphql/models.py, src/back/core/graphql/__init__.py
   Compact per-type digest (root fields, attributes, relationships with
   labels, inverse fields) memoised on SchemaMetadata, so it is cached per
   domain with the schema; shrinks attribute detail to stay under 9,000
   chars (29-class demo ontology: 8.7 KB vs 23 KB SDL). New constants
   DEFAULT_LIST_LIMIT / MAX_LIST_LIMIT / INVERSE_MAX_ROWS / MAX_DIGEST_CHARS.
8. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
   System prompt rewritten around a fast path: one query_graphql call on the
   fact type with relationship filters / inverse fields for entity-centric
   questions, rows + <list>Count + distinctBy in the same request for
   filtered lists, describe_entity only for single-entity profiles at the
   default depth (the "depth >= 2" advice is removed), omit entity_type when
   unsure, group by entity id on name collisions, Count/filters for
   aggregations and an explicit "use Genie/SQL" hand-off for sums/rankings,
   answers capped at ~10 rows plus totals with partial results flagged.
   New build_system_prompt() and run_agent(schema_digest=...) inject the
   digest per turn.
9. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/tools.py
   query_graphql gets its own 32,000-char cap (one or two GraphQL calls per
   turn on the fast path; a complete ~110-row list with nested refs + uris
   is ~20-27k chars); truncation notes now say the result is PARTIAL and
   point to Count. Tool descriptions aligned with the digest / filters.
10. src/agents/tools/graph_formatting.py
   format_graphql_response renders one line per entity
   ("label [id] <uri> | field=value | rel=..."), long nested lists as
   sub-rows, and a "distinct <rel>: N" summary per root list. A 110-row
   fact list with three nested refs is 13.8k chars (was >20k at 200 rows).
11. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   _chat_schema_digest() builds the digest from the cached session schema
   and both Graph Chat routes pass it to run_agent; /dtwin/graphql/schema
   also returns "digest". The /sync/filter route is untouched.
12. tests/eval/datasets/agent_dtwin_chat/regression.jsonl (new),
    .planning/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/SPEC.md
   Two production-derived regression examples (the two traced questions)
   and the SPEC regression section.
14. src/agents/tools/graph_formatting.py (KRW units)
   An internal evaluation run showed replies with 10-100x KRW -> 억
   conversion errors when the model converted units itself. New with_krw_unit / krw_eok_text: every
   field whose name ends in "krw" (any case) gets a deterministic 억 value
   next to the raw number, plus 만원 below 1억
   (`grossKrw: 1409235 (0.014억, 140.9만원)`), in GraphQL rows,
   describe_entity attributes, dataset rows and action result rows.
15. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py (prompt + token bloat)
   Prompt rules: copy the tool's 억 value and never convert units
   (1억 = 100,000,000 KRW); never add up / average / count sampled rows;
   for aggregates check pre-aggregated *Summary / *Performance / *Target
   types first, then aliased Count fields per group. New
   compact_tool_messages(): before each LLM call, tool results of the
   latest assistant turn plus the newest 2 stay in full and older ones are
   cut to their first 1,500 chars with a "[compacted ...]" note (baseline
   median 132k / max 545k prompt tokens per question). Works on a copy;
   order, roles and tool_call_id pairing are unchanged.
16. Tests:
   tests/units/api/test_graphql_relationship_queries.py (new) builds the
   schema from a Customer / Product / SalesOrganization / SalesChannel /
   SalesTransaction ontology and runs the real generated SQL on in-memory
   SQLite: inverse SDL + resolution, cycles / self-reference / collision,
   relationship / data / id filters, AND semantics, counts + distinctBy,
   selection-aware loading, legacy eager path, the two production questions
   end to end, formatter compactness, digest content / cap and the route
   helper. tests/units/core/test_graph_store_subject_filters.py (new) pins
   the inverse / filter / count SQL incl. escaping.
   tests/units/graphdb/test_neo4j_subject_filters.py (new) covers the
   Cypher variants. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py and
   tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat.py cover the prompt (digest
   injection, no "depth >= 2", filters/count docs, unit-conversion rule),
   the GraphQL cap, and tool-history compaction (older results compacted at
   iteration k, latest parallel batch kept whole, tool_call_id pairing
   intact, input not mutated). tests/units/agents/test_graph_formatting_krw.py
   (new) checks the two baseline amounts (11.44억, 197.48억) and 0.014억.

